	Section:
		Text: Styles
			Style: topic
		Heading 1:
			Text: For element
		Text: A rule in `Styles` gives properties to many elements at once. `For element: Paragraph` gives every `Paragraph` of the document the serif font, the justified lines and the blue rule on the left. A `Text` is another type of element, and the rule leaves it alone (this explanation is a `Text` too).
			Style: intro
		Text: For element: Paragraph
			Style: label
		Paragraph: The market returns to the main square on Saturday with more stalls than ever: vegetables from the market gardens, cheese from the hills and wood-fired bread.
		Paragraph: The residents' association is also organizing a walk along the river, starting from the old bridge at ten in the morning.
		Text: This line is a Text: the rule for paragraphs does not reach it.
			Box:
				Margin: 6 0 0 0
